      "baseline_text": "I need to check the reservation details first. The reservation EUJUY6 is for a round trip from ORD to LAS, with basic economy cabin. It has 3 passengers and travel insurance. The flights are:\n- HAT238: ORD to DEN on 2024-05-14\n- HAT290: DEN to LAS on 2024-05-14\n- HAT266: LAS to IAH on 2024-05-16\n- HAT044: IAH to ORD on 2024-05-16\n\nThe current date is 2024-05-15. Looking at the flight dates, the first two flights (ORD-DEN and DEN-LAS) were on 2024-05-14, which is yesterday. This means those flights have already been flown.\n\nAccording to policy: \"If any portion of the flight has already been flown, the agent cannot help and transfer is needed.\"\n\nSince the first two flights were on 2024-05-14 (yesterday), they have already been flown. Therefore, I cannot modify this reservation and would need to transfer to a human agent.\n\nHowever, let me first confirm the user's request and explain the situation. The user wants to change the date out by 2 days due to their wife passing away. But since portions of the flight have already been flown, I cannot make this change.\n\nLet me inform the user about this limitation and that I'll need to transfer them to a human agent.\n</think>\n\n<tool_call>\n<function=transfer_to_human_agents>\n<parameter=summary>\nUser Lucas Brown (lucas_brown_4047) wants to change the date of reservation EUJUY6 by moving it out 2 days due to his wife's tragic passing. However, the reservation contains flights that have already been flown (ORD-DEN and DEN-LAS on 2024-05-14, which was yesterday). According to policy, if any portion of the flight has already been flown, the agent cannot help and transfer is needed. User is extremely distraught but insists on changing the date rather than cancelling.\n</parameter>\n</function>\n",
